(7623899, 1234984, 96574, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by roz:</b></div><hr/><i> congratulations on the yellow ribbon .. this was my absolute fav in the challenge .. the sort of photo i wish i could take .. beautiful light and colours .. and like i said in voting .. STUNNING .. !! .. added caps now ... <br/> <br/>it appears .. from the comments ..  that you have been away for a few months ... i was for a few years  .. and came back for the league .. which got me fired up .. so i''m a bit obsessed with dpc right now ... lol .. <br/>anyway ... thankyou so much for your lovely comment on my robberfly .. insects are a very misunderstood lot .. to me they are endlessly fascinating and pretty damn attractive .. i probably get as much joy photographing them as you do photographing your amazing scenery ..  !! .. ;) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Roz!  Definitely likewise that I wish I could take macro photos of insects like you do, they are just fascinating to see and youre a master at it.  Like you the DPL brought me back here but it kind of fried me instead, hehe.  This entry was the first photo Ive taken since the last challenge of the DPL.  Hopefully Ill make it here more often.</td>', 'Originally posted by roz: congratulations on the yellow ribbon .. this was my absolute fav in the challenge .. the sort of photo i wish i could take .. beautiful light and colours .. and like i said in voting .. STUNNING .. !! .. added caps now ...  it appears .. from the comments ..  that you have been away for a few months ... i was for a few years  .. and came back for the league .. which got me fired up .. so i''m a bit obsessed with dpc right now ... lol .. anyway ... thankyou so much for your lovely comment on my robberfly .. insects are a very misunderstood lot .. to me they are endlessly fascinating and pretty damn attractive .. i probably get as much joy photographing them as you do photographing your amazing scenery ..  !! .. ;)   Thanks Roz!  Definitely likewise that I wish I could take macro photos of insects like you do, they are just fascinating to see and youre a master at it.  Like you the DPL brought me back here but it kind of fried me instead, hehe.  This entry was the first photo Ive taken since the last challenge of the DPL.  Hopefully Ill make it here more often.', '2019-04-08 05:14:10.000000', NULL, 0),
