(7623972, 1235140, 50695, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jerryc12:</b></div><hr/><i> If the person is your subject, shouldn''t he be in focus and not so dark. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>since you phrased it as a question, the answer is no.</td>', 'Originally posted by jerryc12: If the person is your subject, shouldn''t he be in focus and not so dark.   since you phrased it as a question, the answer is no.', '2019-04-08 16:40:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(7624005, 1234795, 83313, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by gzupruk:</b></div><hr/><i> This was taken from an airplane window shortly after takeoff from LGA. There was a good bit of haze in the air and some on the window glass as well. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thanks for the info. I don''t like sitting with that camera in a cramped seat for 2 or 3 hours, but I''ve gotten some good shots out of it and sometimes regretted leaving it in my backback in the overhead.</td>', 'Originally posted by gzupruk: This was taken from an airplane window shortly after takeoff from LGA. There was a good bit of haze in the air and some on the window glass as well.  Thanks for the info. I don''t like sitting with that camera in a cramped seat for 2 or 3 hours, but I''ve gotten some good shots out of it and sometimes regretted leaving it in my backback in the overhead.', '2019-04-08 21:35:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(7624009, 1235140, 38162, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jerryc12:</b></div><hr/><i> If the person is your subject, shouldn''t he be in focus and not so dark. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>since you phrased it as a question, the answer is no. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Well, I wanted him to be just another part of furniture backstage, but a human one to add mystery.  I had no control over the guy so it worked out this way.<br/>Thanks<br/>Jim</td>', 'Originally posted by posthumous: Originally posted by jerryc12: If the person is your subject, shouldn''t he be in focus and not so dark.   since you phrased it as a question, the answer is no.   Well, I wanted him to be just another part of furniture backstage, but a human one to add mystery.  I had no control over the guy so it worked out this way.ThanksJim', '2019-04-08 21:45:17.000000', NULL, 0),
